@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Busy}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Overview}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Overview</h1>


<p>
    The Busy Indicator component displays a spinner to indicate that an action is currently in progress, such as retrieving or saving data.
    This implementation differs from most others in several ways:
</p>
<ol>
    <li>
        Everything beneath the indicator (excluding the trigger button) is made inert, rendering it inaccessible to all users until the action completes.
    </li>
    <li>
        The component can be configured to cover the entire page or just a specific section of it.
    </li>
    <li>
        Users with reduced motion enabled on their device will see a static hourglass instead of a spinning circle.
    </li>
    <li>
        It requires you to provide a message that is dispatched via the Live Region Service (part of the BlazorRamp.Core package) 
        to hidden ARIA live regions, allowing assistive technologies such as screen readers to announce the current status to their users.
    </li>
</ol>


<section class="info-box info-box--container-test" style="margin-top:2rem;">
    <BusyIndicator ShowIndicator="@_showTestIndicator" BusyText=". . . Saving, please wait . . ." IndicatorTrigger="Test Busy Indicator Button"
                   AriaEndText="@_ariaEndText" ContentPosition="ContentPosition.Centre" OverlayPosition=" OverlayPosition.Container">
        <p>
            <b>Try it:</b> This text is inside a container (<span class="@CodeSpan.Base">position:relative</span>).I have set the indicator to be top of the container, with the
            optional <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">aria-hidden</span> text of "Saving, please wait", using a dummy async Task set for <b>2 seconds</b> (the actual time taken is slightly longer given additional timings for clearing announcements).
        </p>
        <p>
            I have set the required <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">AriaEndText</span> to "Saved, successfully" which is sent via the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">LiveRegionService</span> for screen readers to announce. 
            Click the Alerts button, bottom right of the page after trying the busy indicator.This text has been wrapped by the busy indicator as sometimes it makes it clearer to do this so you can see which blocks of code 
            the busy indicator is protecting when wading through your html.
        </p>
        <p>
            Everything behind the overlay is inert excluding the triggering button.
        </p>
        <button class="test-button" role="button" @onclick="RunDummyTask">Test Busy Indicator</button>
    </BusyIndicator>
</section>

<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Announcement}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Announcement - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Busy}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Installation}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Busy - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Installation</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>

@code {
    private bool _showTestIndicator = false;
    private string _ariaEndText = String.Empty;

    private async Task RunDummyTask()
    {
        _showTestIndicator = true;

        await Task.Delay(2000);

        _ariaEndText = "Saved successfully";
        _showTestIndicator = false;
    }
}



